      "answer": "To determine the area of your rectangular painting in square metres, you need to know the length and width of the painting. The formula for the area \\( A \\) of a rectangle is: \\[ A = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} \\] Here are the steps to calculate the area: 1. Measure the length of the painting. Let's say the length is \\( l \\) metres.\n2. Measure the width of the painting. Let's say the width is \\( w \\) metres.\n3. Multiply the length by the width to get the area. For example, if the length of the painting is 5 metres and the width is 3 metres, the area would be: \\[ A = 5 \\, \\text{metres} \\times 3 \\, \\text{metres} = 15 \\, \\text{square metres} \\] So, the area of your rectangular painting is \\(\\boxed{15}\\) square metres.\n\nUnverified. The local model supplied this answer.\n",
